# Lean build outputs and fetched dependencies. Upstream Lean convention is that the whole `.lake/`
# directory is generated: `.lake/build/` holds compiled artifacts and `.lake/packages/` holds the
# sources `lake` fetches from `lake-manifest.json`. 65 files under `.lake/build/` were tracked until
# 2026-09-22, which is why every session opened on hundreds of modified files and a real change was
# hard to spot among them — `lake build` regenerates all of it.
/proofs/lean/.lake/

# Built binaries that live beside their crate rather than at the root (the root-level names are
# covered above; these are the same programs built in place).
/bin/dwowd/dwowd
/bin/dww/dwow_wallet

# Ad-hoc compiler output
a.out

# The status report's raw instrument capture. `reports/status-<date>.md` IS tracked — it is evidence, and
# `scripts/check-register-artifacts.sh` requires a row that cites an artefact to have it in HEAD. The raw
# directory beside it is the verbatim stdout/stderr/exit of each instrument: regenerable in seconds by
# re-running `scripts/report-status.sh`, and large, so it is not. The extensions are deliberately not
# `.md`: `scripts/check-doc-index.sh` globs the WORKING TREE (`:121-126`), so a `.md` written here would
# enter the doc gate's scope whether or not it is tracked.
/reports/*.raw/
